WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
A new analysis of eight major randomized trials shows mammograms lead to far less breast cancer over diagnosis than earlier estimates suggested. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 196. Looking back over the past week, several threads stood out across episodes. One involved AI models that decoded chest x-rays from millions of people and predicted cancers well before diagnosis. Another followed how more time in REM sleep tracked with lower risk

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.840
across dozens of diseases in a large adult cohort.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:39.440
A third showed worms given magnetotactic bacteria lived substantially longer than controls.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.980
A researcher reexamined all eight major randomized screening trials for breast cancer.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:50.980
Differences in follow-up time, screening frequency, and post-trial screening were accounted for

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.960
in the reanalysis.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.260
The resulting overdiagnosis rate fell below 5%.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:02.140
That stands in contrast to some earlier estimates that placed rates near 30-50%.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.360
The uniform adjustments across every included trial produce the consistent lower figure.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.480
Source material appears in Science Daily.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.040
Blocking the growth hormone receptor produced lifespan extension in mice.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:19.320
The work is described as a landmark finding in aging biology.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.900
The intervention targets a receptor pathway known to influence aging processes in rodent

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:25.260
models.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:25.440
samples.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.800
Additional experiments examine the receptor across different mouse strains.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.040
The study appears through bioengineer.org.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.460
Researchers from Rotslav University of Environmental and Life Sciences tested a natural enzyme from

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.340
FigLeaf Gourd.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.240
The enzyme weakened recognition of peanut proteins by antibodies involved in allergic reactions.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.640
Laboratory tests applied the enzyme directly to the protein samples.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.100
Peanut allergy ranks among the most serious food allergies because of potential life-threatening

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:56.600
reactions.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.020
The enzyme source was Cucurbita Ficopholia.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.680
The report comes from Fizz.org.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:08.560
Scented cleaners react with ozone to create billions or trillions of invisible nanoparticles.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.420
These particles form within minutes in typical indoor air.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.680
They can penetrate deep into the lungs.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:20.360
In some scenarios, the inhaled particle dose matches or exceeds levels near heavy traffic.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.580
The reaction uses ozone already present in indoor environments.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.860
Details are in science daily.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.800
Artificial intelligence has produced global weather models that rival physics-based systems

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.780
for many forecasts.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.420
AI still has difficulty predicting the fury of hurricane intensity.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:44.180
The limitation shows most clearly when models attempt to forecast rapid changes in storm

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:50.700
strength. Physics-based systems retain an edge in those intensity scenarios. The account is from

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:58.000
Fizz.org. A researcher followed 80 young people with vision impairment over 11 years. The study

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.480
tracked their journeys from school into adulthood through regular interviews. It documented what had

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:09.020
gone well and what could have been improved in support systems. The longitudinal design allowed

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:15.320
repeated contact at multiple life stages. Persistent gaps in transition services after secondary

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:22.620
education emerged as a key finding. The report is from Fizz.org. The signature was once thought to

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.480
record a massive global change in Earth's carbon cycle. The discovery raises new questions about

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:34.740
conditions when oxygen transformed the young planet. The alternative explanation centers on localized

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.140
geological and biological processes.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.780
Updated geochemical methods were applied to samples from the original site.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.060
Science Daily carries the account.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:50.600
Scientists used a 13-ion quantum simulator to recreate a particle forming process linked

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.880
to the extreme physics of the early universe.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.680
The simulator reproduced conditions associated with rapid particle creation after the initial

00:03:58.680 --> 00:03:59.280
expansion.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.540
Each ION served as a controllable quantum bit within the experimental array.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:10.380
The results demonstrate that current quantum hardware can model specific high-energy processes.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:15.760
The work suggests quantum computers could eventually help investigate how matter-formed

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:16.720
after the Big Bang.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:23.780
Science Daily reports the study, scientists rejuvenated brain cells that stored old memories, making

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.440
those memories accessible again.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.800
The work focuses on end-grammed cells and their functional restoration in aged brains.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:37.680
The intervention targeted cellular states within memory networks rather than replacing entire cell populations.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.440
Aged models showed renewed ability to retrieve previously formed memories after treatment.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:49.640
The approach highlights that some memory deficits may arise from reversible changes in existing neurons.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.400
Popular mechanics covers the findings.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:59.540
Tear Zepatide, sold as Mount Jarrow and Zepbound, activated calorie-burning brown fat in obese

00:04:59.540 --> 00:04:59.880
mice.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.040
The activation occurred in addition to known effects on food intake.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:09.480
Researchers measured increased energy expenditure tied directly to the brown fat response.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.480
The finding reveals a potential metabolic effect beyond appetite suppression.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.300
Confirmation in humans could help explain the drug's benefits.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.000
Science Daily reports the mouse study.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:26.940
Nina Nizar initiated development of a drug for Janssen's Metaphysial Condor Displasia.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:32.580
After discovering her children shared the rare genetic disorder, she became the first participant

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.140
in the resulting human trial.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:38.940
Her advocacy moved research from scientific concept to a potential treatment.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.820
The disorder affects skeletal development and had remained without targeted therapy.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:49.220
Nizar's personal experience with undiagnosed symptoms drove the push for clinical testing.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.220
The account appears in the week.in.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.460
A study examined Instagram content on women's health topics.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.160
Four out of ten posts were advertisements.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:04.000
The proportion remained consistent across sample accounts focused on women's health.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.700
Many posts presented symptoms without distinguishing between promotional and informational content.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:15.000
The finding highlights the commercial nature of much of the information users encounter on

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:21.900
Perry, Menopause. Fizz.org carries the study. Lucentel forecasts the global longevity ingredient

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:28.500
market will reach $2.1 billion by 2035. The projection covers ingredients positioned

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:34.000
for healthy aging applications. Market growth assumptions include continued research into

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.700
compounds that target age-related processes. The forecast period spans from the current year

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:47.260
through 2035. The report is from OpenPR.com. A paper reports that muscle fiber atrophy during

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:52.480
aging and disuse is mainly associated with a lower number of myocybrals rather than

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:59.120
smaller myocybral size. The distinction points to a reduction in contractile unit quantity rather

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:05.080
than shrinkage of existing units. Data were collected from both aging and immobilization models.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.520
The results refine understanding of how muscle mass declines over time.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:14.780
The paper is available through Fizzoc.onlinelibrary.wiley.com.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:20.780
The gene therapy work on N-gram cells shows that rejuvenating specific memory storing neurons

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:25.120
can restore access to previously inaccessible memories in aged models.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:30.560
This approach targets cellular function within the brain's memory networks, rather than broad

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:31.480
tissue replacement.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:36.860
It opens a path toward interventions that address selective memory loss without requiring

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:38.340
full neural regeneration.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:44.360
The technique demonstrates that some age-related memory deficits may stem from reversible cellular

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.520
states rather than permanent loss of the cells themselves.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:52.780
One open question is how long the restored access persists after treatment.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:57.680
Most people assume that once the scent of a cleaner fades, the air is back to normal.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:03.180
Right now, as you move through a recently cleaned room, your lungs may still be encountering

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.900
particles created minutes earlier.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:10.180
Researchers measured that scented cleaners reacting with indoor ozone produce billions

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:14.660
or trillions of nanoparticles small enough to reach deep lung tissue.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:21.340
In some scenarios, the total particle dose of person-inhales equals or exceeds standing beside

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.160
heavy traffic.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:29.500
The process begins when volatile compounds from the cleaner meet ozone molecules already present in typical indoor air.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:35.080
Ventilation after cleaning remains the most direct step anyone can take to reduce exposure.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:43.800
Before we go, keep an eye on further work that tests whether the brown fat activation seen with tears epitide holds in human studies.

